# PLAN-1093 — the prepared foreign language surface (use.rs / use.c) through the ordinary AV chain

Provider sources are FROZEN: the Rust `f0_text/1` provider
(`abi/rustside/f0_text.rs`) and the C provider `parity1093_c` (annotated
header + unit; `parity1093_c_impl.c` binds the REAL `<string.h>` strlen
with the full SDK include closure). The ordinary worker loads PREPARED
provider closures only — no compiler runs in a daily case.

## Case: rust-length-not-strlen
id: "av.parity.1093.rust-length-not-strlen"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1093"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
use.rs f0_text
fn main() int { return text_byte_len("A中😀\0") }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "f0_text" }
exit: 9

#### stdout

```text
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

The UTF-8 byte length is 9 — by BYTES, never C-strlen-truncated to the
first NUL. Real Rust provider dispatch through the ordinary AV chain; the
provider closure identity binds the frozen f0_text source.

