## Case: explicit-c-library
id: "av.parity.1093.explicit-c-library"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1093"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
use.c parity1093_c
fn main() int { return c_strlen("hello") }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "c", provider: "parity1093_c" }
exit: 5

#### stdout

```text
```

#### stderr

```text
```

### Notes

Explicit C external library: the provider unit calls the REAL `<string.h>`
strlen (SDK-closure compile); the AV side passes the borrowed view as the
(data, len) pair and the C side builds the bounded C string (the CStr
bridge). Not a default-stdlib path.

## Case: rust-missing-capability
id: "av.parity.1093.rust-missing-capability"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1093"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
use.rs f0_text
fn main() int { return text_byte_len("hi") }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "rust", provider: "f0_text" }
stage: "resolve"
code: "source.foreign-capability"

### Notes

A foreign import without the explicit `foreign.scalar` capability is a
named bind-stage rejection with the source span — the import cannot widen
authority the case did not declare.

## Case: c-header-spelling-rejected
id: "av.parity.1093.c-header-spelling-rejected"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1093"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
use.c <string.h>
fn main() int { return c_strlen("hello") }
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "foreign.scalar", "foreign.resource", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
foreign: { kind: "c", provider: "parity1093_c" }
stage: "resolve"
code: "source.use-rs.provider"

### Notes

The `use.c <string.h>` header spelling parses (the C header import form),
but the admitted provider is `parity1093_c` — the import cannot invent or
widen a provider the host did not admit.
